;a way to implement quicksort is this:
make two arrows, high and low
high starts pointing at last element and low and first
store the element at low and make a hole in its place
the arrow not pointing to a hole, high, moves towards the array center
it moves through the elements until it sees an element higher than the one stored
it puts that number in the hole, moves low 1 step forward
and makes a hole in place of high
now the arrow not pointing to a hole, 
low starts moving until it finds an element lower than the one stored
then it puts the element at low in the hole, moves high forward
and high starts moving
until low and high point towards the same hole at the end
